meta {
  name: Delete category
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/1
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Delete a category

  Soft delete: sets `status` to 0 and `statusName` to `INACTIVE`, and records who did it in `updated`. The row stays in the database but disappears from every read.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Path parameters

  | Name | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | integer | yes | Positive integer. |

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

    {
      "message": "Category deleted",
      "data": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "pagination": null
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  `id` is not a positive integer.

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "id",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 404 Not Found — no active category with this id

  Soft-deleted records answer 404 too.

    {
      "message": "Category not found.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
